nodecode-bubblewrap is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
  commit e7a218f26db88426ab3e7376f0e000b6e356f5e7 (plugin folder bubblewrap)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (LICENSE)

cell.lisp is the original's sandbox.py, __init__.py and home.py rewritten as a
Nodecode cell: the bwrap argv it builds (unshare-all, die-with-parent,
new-session, a read-only root, one writable directory, a fresh /dev, /proc and
/tmp, /run/user emptied, the agent sockets removed from the environment), the
home directory rule that hides the dot entries off an allowlist and the
credential stores always, the three profiles, the memory and CPU limits in front
of bwrap and the process limit inside it, and the probe that says whether
unprivileged user namespaces work. The original's prompt note (where the
boundary is, and to report it rather than work around it) is the manual topic
(help :bubblewrap), rewritten for a harness whose file tools run in the same
image.

Left out, because Nodecode has no terminal-backend seam to plug into:

  - the original ran every terminal and execute_code call of the harness inside
    the box; this cell offers the box as two tools (sandbox, sandbox_status) and
    the verb (bubblewrap:sandbox "..."), which a model or an operator calls.
  - the Hermes home, the scratch directory and its per-session state directory,
    which are Hermes' own paths.
  - the CA-bundle bind-back, the per-sandbox scratch directory that survives a
    sandbox (this cell's /tmp is fresh per command), background jobs, and the
    file-tool sandboxing, which are the harness' rather than the box's.
  - extra binds are mounted read-only or read-write at their own path (two
    lists) instead of the original's {src, dest, readonly} objects, so a bind at
    a different destination is not carried over.

The tests are Nodecode's: a stubbed host (paths, home listing, process runner),
so nothing in them starts bwrap or reads a real home directory.
